  "notes": "The Ministry of Education's Plano Sectorial da Educação 2017-2025 confirms basic education in three cycles for ages 6–14: the 1st and 2nd cycles take six years (ages 6–11), the 3rd is 7º–9º ano with a national exam after 9º ano, and secondary runs to 12º ano. The 4+2 split of the first six years is from the ISCED 2011 mapping for Guinea-Bissau cited here, which dates entry at 6 from 2010-11. The plan names years 'ano'; the 'classe' names used here are not confirmed by an official source."
